#: ../../source/heartmula_SKILL.md:93
msgid "GPU / CUDA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/heartmula_SKILL.md:95
msgid ""
"HeartMuLa uses CUDA by default (`--mula_device cuda --codec_device "
"cuda`). No extra setup needed if the user has an NVIDIA GPU with PyTorch "
"CUDA support installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/heartmula_SKILL.md:97
msgid "The installed `torch==2.4.1` includes CUDA 12.1 support out of the box"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/heartmula_SKILL.md:98
msgid ""
"`torchtune` may report version `0.4.0+cpu` — this is just package "
"metadata, it still uses CUDA via PyTorch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/heartmula_SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"To verify GPU is being used, look for \"CUDA memory\" lines in the output"
" (e.g. \"CUDA memory before unloading: 6.20 GB\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/heartmula_SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"**No GPU?** You can run on CPU with `--mula_device cpu --codec_device "
"cpu`, but expect generation to be **extremely slow** (potentially 30-60+ "
"minutes for a single song vs ~4 minutes on GPU). CPU mode also requires "
"significant RAM (~12GB+ free). If the user has no NVIDIA GPU, recommend "
"using a cloud GPU service (Google Colab free tier with T4, Lambda Labs, "
"etc.) or the online demo at https://heartmula.github.io/ instead."
msgstr ""

